Model weights: origin and attributions
--------------------------------------
The Ito model was designed and trained by Lokutor. It learned from speech generated by a teacher model; no
third-party weights are included in it.

- Teacher: StyleTTS 2 by Yinghao Aaron Li et al., https://github.com/yl4579/StyleTTS2, with its public pretrained
  checkpoints (https://huggingface.co/yl4579), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023 Aaron (Yinghao) Li. The teacher was used
  to generate training data. Its code and weights are not included here.
  StyleTTS 2's authors ask users of their pretrained models to tell listeners that the speech is synthesized, unless
  the speaker whose voice is synthesized has given permission. Ito's voice comes from that teacher, so we pass the
  same request on: please disclose that Ito's output is synthetic speech.
- Voices: for each Ito voice the teacher was conditioned on recordings of one speaker of LibriTTS-R (Yuma Koizumi et
  al., 2023; https://www.openslr.org/141/), licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/):
    female voice (the default): LibriTTS-R speaker 4970;
    male voice:                   LibriTTS-R speaker 5105.
  LibriTTS-R derives from LibriTTS (Heiga Zen et al., 2019), which derives from LibriVox public-domain recordings.
  Each Ito voice imitates the voice of its LibriTTS-R speaker, a LibriVox volunteer reader. Ito is not affiliated with
  or endorsed by those speakers, LibriVox, or Google. No recordings are redistributed here.
- Input text given to the teacher: transcripts from DisfluencySpeech
  (https://huggingface.co/datasets/amaai-lab/DisfluencySpeech, Apache License 2.0), and LJSpeech sentence text (public
  domain). Only text was used; none of it is redistributed here.

